This is based on the assumption each of the tests (PexMethods) always run successfully and will not throw exceptions. The tests are assuming certain conditions to always execute successfully and therefore are not covering all possible scenarios. For example, `PUT_ContainsContract` could fail if `x` is removed from the ArrayList. It is also missing several assert conditions because we were unable to determine all necessary conditions for them to always succeed in a safe manner for Pex's safety checks. Also, some conditions depend on assumptions being true and might have undesired behaviors in real application.--------------------
